  "_inferred": "Motor Kv and resistance, ESC parameters and airframe drag areas are NOT published. The rotor figure of merit is the one number that matters most for a hover check, and it is left blank, so the model uses its default for a 21 in rotor (0.78) rather than a tuned value.",
  "_calibration": "Nothing is tuned. The judgement calls are usable capacity, set to the conventional 80% rather than the 90% first tried (DJI does not say what state of charge its 55 min is measured to, and no operator lands a Matrice at 10%), and the rotor figure of merit, left at the default for the diameter. Counting propulsion only, the model gives 51.0 min against a published 55; between figures of merit of 0.75 and 0.80 it gives 49.3 to 52.1 min. The pack energy matches exactly at 548 Wh, which is the battery model agreeing with DJI arithmetic rather than anything being fitted.\n\nThe avionics rails below add about 72 W, which DJI does not publish; with them, as the GUI runs this file, the hover is 42.7 min. Edit them if you know the real draw.\n\nBefore audit M13 the model priced the rotor as ideal and took the motor's copper loss off its input power, and gave 55.2 min: right by a cancellation of errors that did not survive scaling down to the M30."
